  "content": {
    "id": "p29-q08-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "If the amount of Karlima’s savings is squared and then doubled, the amount would be $\\$66$ more than her savings now. How much has she saved?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$6$",
      "worked": "Let $s$ be Karlima’s savings in dollars, where $s\\geq0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2s^2&=s+66\\\\2s^2-s-66&=0\\\\(s-6)(2s+11)&=0\\\\s&=6\\text{ or }-\\frac{11}{2}.\\end{align*}$$\nReject $s=-\\frac{11}{2}$ because her savings cannot be negative. Karlima has saved $\\$6$.\n\nCheck: $2(6)^2=72=6+66$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 50
  },
